  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "This problem has the same setup as `KUPSETMN`. The only difference is that here, you need to create exactly KKK upsets in the tournament.\n\nYou are given three integers N,K,N, K,N,K, and WWW.\n\nConstruct any array AAA of length 2N+1−12^{N+1}-12N+1−1 satisfying the following properties:\n\n\nA1=WA_1 = WA1​=W.\nFor each 1≤i&lt;2N1 \\le i \\lt 2^N1≤i&lt;2N, either Ai=max⁡(A2i,A2i+1)A_i = \\max(A_{2i}, A_{2i+1})Ai​=max(A2i​,A2i+1​) or Ai=min⁡(A2i,A2i+1)A_i = \\min(A_{2i}, A_{2i+1})Ai​=min(A2i​,A2i+1​).\nThere are exactly KKK indices among these for which Ai=max⁡(A2i,A2i+1)A_i = \\max(A_{2i}, A_{2i+1})Ai​=max(A2i​,A2i+1​).\nThe last 2N2^N2N elements of AAA form a permutation of {1,2,…,2N}\\{1, 2, \\ldots, 2^N\\}{1,2,…,2N}.\nLess formally, you are to set up a single-elimination tournament bracket on players labeled {1,2,…,2N}\\{1, 2, \\ldots, 2^N\\}{1,2,…,2N} such that the eventual winner of the tournament is WWW, and there are exactly KKK upsets across the entire tournament; where an upset is defined to be a player with larger label defeating a player with smaller label.\n\nIf there are multiple possible solutions, you may find any of them.\n\nIf there's no solution, output the single integer −1-1−1.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of a single line of input, containing three space-separated integers N,K,N, K,N,K, and WWW.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case,\n\n\n\nIf no solution exists, output the single integer −1-1−1 on a new line.\nOtherwise, output 2N+1−12^{N+1}-12N+1−1 space-separated integers denoting the array you found.\n\nIf there are multiple possible solutions, you may find any of them.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤171 \\leq N \\leq 171≤N≤17",
      "0≤K&lt;2N0 \\le K \\lt 2^N0≤K&lt;2N",
      "1≤W≤2N1 \\le W \\le 2^N1≤W≤2N",
      "The sum of 2N2^N2N over all test cases won't exceed 2172^{17}217."
    ],
